-api failing health checks after v2.3.1 deploy - rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api began failing health checks after the v2.3.1 production deploy (error rate 0.18). Actions taken: rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. The first rollback attempt halted after us-east with an orchestrator error (partial failure, leaving the service mixed across regions). I retried the rollback and it completed in all regions: us-east, us-west, and eu-west are now on v2.3.0. Post-rollback status: healthy, error rate 0.002. v2.3.1 is marked unhealthy in production and v2.3.1-rc is marked unhealthy in staging. Follow-up: investigate the v2.3.1 failure and the orchestrator error that halted the first rollback attempt.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-sev2-rollback-v2.3.0-2025"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "checkout-api is rolled back to v2.3.0 in all three regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). It is healthy again with an error rate of 0.002, down from 0.18.\n\n- **Rollback target:** v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production. v2.3.1 was the unhealthy release.\n- **Rollout issue:** The first rollback attempt halted after us-east with an orchestrator error, leaving the service mixed across regions. I retried the same rollback and it completed everywhere.\n- **Incident:** I opened SEV2 incident INC-0001 for checkout-api, which paged on-call. The first incident request timed out, so I retried with the same idempotency key. The incident was opened once.\n\nThe incident summary covers the rollback, the partial failure, and the follow-up work: investigating the v2.3.1 failure and the orchestrator error. v2.3.1-rc is also marked unhealthy in staging and was not touched.", "type": "text"}]}]}